==Icelandic==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|non|is}} {{term|eyra|lang=non}}, from the voiced Verner alternant of {{etyl|gem-pro|is}} {{term/t|gem-pro|*ausô}}, from {{etyl|ine-pro|is}} {{term/t|ine-pro|*h₂ous-}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈeiːra/|lang=is}}
*: {{rhymes|eiːra|lang=is}}
*: Homophones: {{l|is|eira}}

===Noun===
{{is-noun|n|eyra|eyru}}

# [[ear]] (organ of hearing)
#* [[w:en:Hávamál|Hávamál]] ([[s:en:Poetic Edda/Hávamál|English source]], [[s:is:Hávamál|Icelandic sourve]])
#*: ''Inn vari gestur''
#*: ''er til verðar kemur''
#*: ''[[þegja þunnu hljóði|þunnu hljóði þegir]],''
#*: '''''eyrum''' hlýðir,''
#*: ''en augum skoðar.''
#*: ''Svo nýsist fróðra hver fyrir.''
#*:: The knowing guest
#*:: who goes to the feast,
#*:: In silent attention sits;
#*:: With his '''ears''' he hears, 
#*:: with his eyes he watches,
#*:: Thus wary are wise men all. 

